   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number and quality of local returnee reintegration strategies components implemented including number of returnees involved in activities aimed at improving their livelihoods, number of returnees accessing mental health support, number of kids reintegrated in the education system</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number and quality of local returnee reintegration strategies components implemented including number of returnees involved in activities aimed at improving their livelihoods, number of returnees accessing mental health support, number of kids reintegrated in the education system</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">N/A</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seventy percent of surveyed clients (service providers and end-beneficairies) satisfied with the quality of delivered services</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Met, per below. 
 Albania- 84% of surveyed respondents  (service providers and end-beneficairies) are very satisfied with the quality of delivered services. A total of 170 survey respondents -returnees and service providers surveyed. 

North Macedonia- 95 % of  surveyed respondents (service providers and end-beneficairies) are very satisfied with the quality of delivered services.  A total of 381 survey respondents-returnees and service providers  surveyed.

Serbia- 94 % of  surveyed respondents  (service providers and end-beneficairies) are very satisfied with the quality of delivered services. A total of 309 survey respondents-returnees and service providers  surveyed&quot;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fifty percent of surveyed clients (service providers and end-beneficairies) satisfied with the quality of delivered services</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Progress, with contextual explanation.
Contextual Explanation: For all 9 municipalities, various components of the reintegration strategies (access to govt. services, employment, education, social cohesion) are currently being implemented. For example, only the Action has reached and assisted over  1740 returnees across 9 partner municipalities with access to services, while the Action is only one part of overall reintegration efforts. As the LAPs for reintegration have been adopted last year and monitoring is  done on one-year-cycles/annually,  with Action support, by Q1 2024 partners will complete the monitoring of the LAP implementation and more accurate reporting will be availbale.
 In addition, for returnees that took part in employability trainings as part of the Action, in N. Macedonia and Serbia, the Action surveyed participants satisfaction and more than 90% were satisfied with the training provided.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
